# WPF MVVM

- Views (`Views/*.xaml`) are layout only. Code-behind may `InitializeComponent` and nothing else unless a view-only quirk requires it.
- One screen → `FooView.xaml` + `FooView.xaml.cs` + `FooWorkspaceViewModel.cs` (or `FooViewModel.cs`). Do not group multiple workspace types in one file.
- ViewModels: CommunityToolkit.Mvvm (`ObservableObject`, `[ObservableProperty]`, `[RelayCommand]`). Expose `ObservableCollection<T>` for grids. Commands call Application services.
- `WorkspaceBase` for loadable screens. Navigation keys match permission screen keys (`customers`, `dispatch-orders`).
- Bind in XAML (`DataContext`, `Command`, `ItemsSource`). Do not reach into named controls from the ViewModel.
- Never use `Plexis.*`, Crystal, or Infragistics. Printing goes through `IDocumentPrinter` in `Hma.Reporting`.
- Register ViewModels as scoped/transient in the desktop host DI; resolve `MainWindow` / `LoginWindow` from the container.

```csharp
// BAD — code-behind
private async void Save_Click(...) => await db.SaveChangesAsync();

// GOOD — ViewModel
[RelayCommand]
private async Task Save(CancellationToken ct) => await _customers.SaveAsync(Editor, ct);
```
